1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:05,000
QRAC.me: post-quantum accounts for Ethereum, working today and ready for EIP-8141.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:12,900
This is QRAC.me in Brave. We start in Dev mode, where every step is visible.

3
00:00:13,607 --> 00:00:18,790
We create a 24-word seed, saved as a file. It is never sent anywhere.

4
00:00:19,340 --> 00:00:25,457
Brave Wallet connects on Sepolia. It only pays gas, with no control over the account.

5
00:00:26,007 --> 00:00:31,171
From the seed: 1,024 one-time hash-based keys (LMS). This is the post-quantum part.

6
00:00:31,721 --> 00:00:39,171
We mint the account through our factory. One confirmation, about 738k gas.

7
00:00:39,721 --> 00:00:47,171
Then we fund it with 0.02 Sepolia ETH.

8
00:00:47,721 --> 00:00:57,171
On Etherscan: our account is a contract, holding 0.02 ETH.

9
00:00:57,721 --> 00:01:03,171
Now we send 0.001 ETH back to the Brave wallet.

10
00:01:03,721 --> 00:01:12,171
The review checks that what we sign is, byte for byte, what the contract verifies.

11
00:01:12,721 --> 00:01:22,871
Signed with one-time key #0. Brave just delivers it and pays the gas.

12
00:01:23,471 --> 00:01:29,071
Etherscan: Brave sent the transaction, and the account paid out 0.001 ETH.

13
00:01:29,271 --> 00:01:34,771
No ECDSA key can move these funds. Only the post-quantum key can.

14
00:01:35,421 --> 00:01:40,586
Now the future: EIP-8141 frame transactions, on the public devnet.

15
00:01:41,136 --> 00:01:48,014
A throwaway setup key gets devnet ETH. It only pays to create and fund the account.

16
00:01:48,564 --> 00:01:56,514
Same seed, new keys for this chain. We mint the account and fund it.

17
00:01:57,114 --> 00:02:01,714
We sign a frame transaction: one post-quantum signature, zero ECDSA.

18
00:02:01,914 --> 00:02:06,414
The check needs about 250k gas, and the account pays its own gas.

19
00:02:07,064 --> 00:02:12,668
The public mempool allows only 100k gas for validation. Rejected.

20
00:02:13,218 --> 00:02:18,577
Each send uses a fresh one-time key, which is also an EIP-8250 nonce key.

21
00:02:19,127 --> 00:02:28,577
The ERC-8421 alternative mempool admits it: 17 of 17 checks. Mined.

22
00:02:29,127 --> 00:02:37,577
The explorer agrees: on chain, the account is the payer, every rule passed.

23
00:02:38,127 --> 00:02:45,577
Same accounts in User mode: a simple wallet anyone can use.

24
00:02:46,127 --> 00:03:01,292
Send, and every step shows live, from the signature to the block.

25
00:03:01,842 --> 00:03:06,292
And on Sepolia, the account we made in Dev mode: 1,015 one-time keys left.

26
00:03:07,092 --> 00:03:14,292
QRAC.me: post-quantum accounts for Ethereum, today. Try it at qrac.me.

